{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"tourmaline-anthracite-robberfly","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Why\n\nTwo regexes key on the `## Success Criteria` heading and one scope extractor lists it. They are\nthe only CODE that reads the heading, so until they change the heading remains load-bearing and\nthe store migration cannot be verified. `_count_ac_items` already counts `- [ ]` items ONLY\nunder `## Acceptance Criteria`, so criteria written under SC never reach the P1 blocking floor\nand can never carry the `[operator-attested]` tag — collapsing the two TIGHTENS the gate.\n\n## What\n\nPoint the heading-reading code at `## Acceptance Criteria`, and update the test fixtures that\nembed `## Success Criteria` in ticket descriptions.\n\n## Scope\n\nCode:\n- `src/rebar/_engine_support/gates.py:136` — the epic branch of `_clarity_score`, currently\n  `+2` for `^##\\s+Success Criteria`.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_floor.py:227` — the deliberate copy of that heuristic used for\n  P1 coverage (non-blocking); the two must stay in lockstep, which the module comments require.\n- `src/rebar/llm/code_review/assemble.py:253` — `_SCOPE_HEADINGS`, which lists\n  `\"## success criteria\"` alongside `\"## acceptance criteria\"`; drop the SC entry.\n\nTest fixtures embedding the heading:\n- `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_gate_rubric_consistency.py:4,36`\n- `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_completion_gate.py:48`\n- `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_gate_subtree.py:28`\n- `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_gate_subtree_heldout.py:22`\n- `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_gate_story_epic.py:29`\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_completion_verifier.py:219,293,356,407,425,465`\n- `tests/unit/test_project_portability_criterion.py:108`\n\nOUT OF SCOPE: removing `clarity-check` entirely (separately planned). This story only stops it\nkeying on the SC heading.\n\n## Approach\n\nIn both `_clarity_score` copies the epic branch becomes a no-op for the SC heading. Because\n`## Acceptance Criteria` is already a universal blocking floor, awarding the epic `+2` for it\nwould make the bonus automatic and the epic branch a no-op discriminator; so the epic branch\nDROPS the heading bonus rather than repointing it, keeping `## Context` as its only remaining\nsignal. This is a deliberate weakening of a metric already slated for removal, recorded here so\nit is a decision rather than an accident.\n\n`_SCOPE_HEADINGS` loses `\"## success criteria\"`; `\"## acceptance criteria\"` already covers the\ncollapsed vocabulary.\n\nFixtures that carry BOTH headings drop the SC block; fixtures carrying SC as their only\ncriteria block have it renamed to `## Acceptance Criteria` with its bullets converted to\n`- [ ]` items so they still satisfy the P1 floor.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `test_gate_rubric_consistency.py` is the invariant that a clarity-PASS implies a check-ac\n  PASS; it must stay green with the epic fixture no longer carrying SC.\n- `pytest tests/interfaces/lifecycle tests/interfaces/store tests/unit/test_project_portability_criterion.py` green.\n- A new case pinning that an epic whose description carries ONLY `## Acceptance Criteria`\n  passes `check-ac` and is claimable — the behaviour the migration depends on.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `grep -rn \"Success Criteria\" src/rebar/_engine_support/gates.py src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_floor.py src/rebar/llm/code_review/assemble.py` returns no matches.\n- [ ] The two `_clarity_score` copies remain textually in lockstep (verified by diffing the two\n      epic branches), preserving the invariant their comments assert.\n- [ ] No test file under `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/`, `tests/interfaces/store/` or\n      `tests/unit/test_project_portability_criterion.py` contains `## Success Criteria`.\n- [ ] A new test asserts an epic with only `## Acceptance Criteria` passes both `clarity-check`\n      and `check-ac` (exit 0 each).\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck` and the full pytest suite pass.","id":"2aa6-726a-ea56-4d6c","parent_id":"1386-5e7c-391d-4a74","priority":2,"tags":["vocabulary","plan-review"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Rename Success Criteria to Acceptance Criteria in reviewer prompts and criteria routing"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1784944744999925001,"uuid":"b719d462-d27b-4402-99b0-c08f01842231"}